.TH TULPAR 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.6.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar \- modern, reliable package manager for APG packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.RI [ arguments... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tulpar
is the command-line package manager for the APG package format,
backed by
.BR libapg (3)
for database storage, dependency resolution, and atomic multi-package
transactions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI help " " [command]
show the usage of tulpar, or of one command; the same as
.B \-\-help
.TP
.BR tulpar-install (1)
install one or more packages from repositories or files (also: i)
.TP
.BR tulpar-remove (1)
remove an installed package (also: uninstall, r)
.TP
.BR tulpar-upgrade (1)
upgrade one or all installed packages (also: u)
.TP
.BR tulpar-search (1)
search local and remote package indexes (also: s)
.TP
.BR tulpar-list (1)
list installed packages (also: l)
.TP
.BR tulpar-info (1)
show full metadata for a package (also: show, n)
.TP
.BR tulpar-verify (1)
verify installed package files against the database (also: v)
.TP
.BR tulpar-orphans (1)
list and remove orphaned packages (also: autoremove, o)
.TP
.BR tulpar-hold (1)
block a package from upgrade or removal (also: g)
.TP
.BR tulpar-unhold (1)
release a held package (also: x)
.TP
.BR tulpar-history (1)
show past install/remove operations (also: audit, log, a)
.TP
.BR tulpar-repo (1)
manage configured repositories (also: e)
.TP
.BR tulpar-download (1)
fetch a package without installing it (also: w)
.TP
.BR tulpar-key (1)
manage the trusted signing keyring (also: k)
.TP
.BR tulpar-graph (1)
export the installed package dependency graph as DOT (also: p)
.TP
.BR tulpar-clean (1)
purge downloaded package archives and metadata cache (also: autoclean, c)
.TP
.BR tulpar-rollback (1)
undo the most recent package operation (also: undo, b)
.TP
.BR tulpar-owns (1)
find the package that owns a file (also: O)
.TP
.BR tulpar-files (1)
list the files of an installed package (also: f)
.TP
.BR tulpar-why (1)
explain why a package is installed (also: W)
.TP
.BR tulpar-mark (1)
mark a package as automatic or explicit (also: m)
.TP
.BR tulpar-reinstall (1)
reinstall installed packages (also: R)
.TP
.BR tulpar-stats (1)
show package database statistics (also: t)
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h \", \" \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V \", \" \-\-version
Show the tulpar version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-y \", \" \-\-yes
Assume yes and skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
.BR \-j \", \" \-\-json
Produce machine-readable JSON output, where supported. The schemas are
described in
.BR tulpar-json (7).
.TP
.BR \-d \", \" \-\-dest \" \" \fIpath\fR
Operate against an alternate filesystem root instead of the live
system. The package database is resolved under
.IR path /var/lib/apg/db
and no root privileges are required, since the destination may be
user-owned.
.TP
.BR \-q \", \" \-\-quiet
Suppress informational output.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable debug output.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Never touch the network. Commands that need it fail with a clear
message, and repository indexes are read from the cache regardless of
its age. Can also be enabled permanently with the
.B offline
key in
.BR tulpar.conf (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " \fIwhen\fR
Colorize output.
.I when
is
.I auto
(the default: color only when the output stream is a terminal),
.IR always ,
or
.IR never .
.TP
.B \-\-require\-signature
Reject packages that fail signature verification instead of only
warning about them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, disables colored output unless
.B \-\-color always
is given.
.TP
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE
When set to a non-empty value, enables colored output even when the
output is not a terminal, unless
.B NO_COLOR
is set or
.B \-\-color never
is given.
.TP
.B TERM
When set to
.IR dumb ,
colored output is disabled in
.I auto
mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apg/tulpar.conf
System-wide configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/apg/tulpar.conf
Per-user configuration override.
.TP
.I /etc/apg/repos.list
System-wide repository URL list.
.TP
.I ~/.config/apg/repos.list
Per-user repository URL list override.
.TP
.I /var/cache/apg/pkgs
Default package cache directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/apg/db
Default LMDB package database directory.
.TP
.I /etc/apg/trusted.d
Default trusted public key directory.
.TP
.I /var/log/tulpar.log
Default log file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar-json (7),
.BR tulpar.conf (5),
.BR libapg (3)
